/node_modules
# dist/ is NOT committed. A `gsx dev` session edits sources live, so any
# committed build output drifts out of parity within minutes — it happened twice.
# `npm ci && npm run build` is a documented prerequisite instead (see README).
# .gitkeep IS tracked: `//go:embed all:dist` fails to build if the directory
# does not exist, so a fresh clone needs it present but empty.
/dist/*
!/dist/.gitkeep
*.x.go
.env
# `go build ./...` at the module root writes a binary named after the
# module directory (not caught by *.x.go or /node_modules above).
/streaming-partial
